Intake channels (Loom AIE2P array plans, constrain.intake %intake, %panel, %offset, %rows, %pitch): a staged binding
multicast reaches each member worker through its streamed panel channel instead of a channel of its own: one memory-tile
ring (own fill channel), drained by the members in order through a lock chain on their panels' memory-tile drain
channels and landed through their panels' receiving DMA in a ring aliasing the idle panel ring (rows |pitch| bytes
apart); every push queues the intake's records ahead of the panel's on both. A fused NPU GEMM's fillers take their
raw weight rows this way instead of reading them from their core stream (~10 cycles a word). The fill and every drain
are terminating chains queued per push, and intake plans start their workers' private storage zeroed, so a re-setup on
a used array starts clean.
